WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.076
Feedback is the mechanism that turns effort into improvement.

00:00:03.076 --> 00:00:03.738
Without feedback,

00:00:03.738 --> 00:00:07.706
the learner may repeat the same approach and mistake familiarity for progress.

00:00:07.706 --> 00:00:11.013
Useful feedback is timely enough to connect to the attempt,

00:00:11.013 --> 00:00:14.651
specific enough to guide correction, and grounded in examples or standards.

00:00:14.651 --> 00:00:19.281
It tells the learner what worked, what did not, and what to try differently.

00:00:19.281 --> 00:00:23.250
Feedback can come from expert coaching, peer review, self-review, worked examples, rubrics,

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:25.565
performance data, or comparison against strong examples.

00:00:25.565 --> 00:00:26.557
In technical work,

00:00:26.557 --> 00:00:30.525
a senior reviewer might explain why one hypothesis was stronger than another.

00:00:30.525 --> 00:00:34.825
In writing, a reviewer might point out where the main claim is buried.

00:00:34.825 --> 00:00:38.463
In leadership, a coach might identify where the conversation lost clarity.

00:00:38.463 --> 00:00:40.777
Correction is the next step after feedback.

00:00:40.777 --> 00:00:44.746
A comment or score is not enough if the learner does not

00:00:44.746 --> 00:00:46.730
adjust the method and try again.

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:50.699
Correction may involve slowing down, using a checklist, practicing a smaller component,

00:00:50.699 --> 00:00:53.345
comparing two examples, or changing the decision rule.

00:00:53.345 --> 00:00:58.305
The value comes from closing the gap between the current performance and the target performance.

00:00:58.305 --> 00:01:01.282
Weak feedback environments create repeated mistakes and false confidence.

00:01:01.282 --> 00:01:05.581
If errors are hidden, delayed, or never connected back to the original action,

00:01:05.581 --> 00:01:09.549
learners can develop habits that feel normal but do not improve results.

00:01:09.549 --> 00:01:12.856
Deliberate practice makes errors visible while they are still correctable.

00:01:12.856 --> 00:01:14.510
That is uncomfortable at times,

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:19.140
but it is much more useful than discovering the same gap during high-stakes work.
